    "body": "## What does this implement/fix?\n\n| Property | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Method | `onCreate` |\n| Class | `com.mine.autoshine.MainActivity` |\n| File | `app/src/main/java/com/mine/autoshine/MainActivity.java` |\n| Specification | `NumberFormatCrashSpec` |\n| Analysis tool | `static:manual` |\n\n## Summary\n\n### Observed dynamic-analysis failure\n\nThe dynamic-analysis run by `static:manual` reported (`NumberFormatCrashSpec`) while exercising `com.mine.autoshine.MainActivity.onCreate`:\n\n> Static candidate (not executed): the Save button listener registered in onCreate calls Integer.parseInt on eight EditText values with no exception handling; the fields use inputType=number, which still allows an empty field and values beyond Integer.MAX_VALUE, so clearing one field and tapping Save throws NumberFormatException and crashes the app (CWE-248).\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe Save listener contains nine direct EditText.getText().toString() to Integer.parseInt operations without a local parser-precondition guard or local recovery. Editable numeric controls do not guarantee non-empty or int-range text, so the parser-input constraint is violated [CLM-002, CLM-003, CLM-004, CLM-005, CLM-006].\n\n### Correction strategy\n\nPreserve successful saves for valid signed-decimal int values. Add a precondition or local failure boundary before assignments, persistence, and broadcast so blank or out-of-range editable values do not reach the nine direct Integer.parseInt calls; invalid-input presentation remains subject to maintainer review.\n\n### Coordinated changes\n\n- `app/src/main/java/com/mine/autoshine/MainActivity.java`: Parse all nine existing EditText values inside a local NumberFormatException boundary before assigning any MySettings fields. Invalid input therefore cannot escape or cause partial mutation, persistence, or broadcast; valid values retain the existing assignments and side-effect order.\n\n## How was this tested?\n\n- No automated test was added in this change\n- [x] Project compiles successfully (`assembleDebug`)\n- [x] Confirmed by a project maintainer\n\n## Additional context\n\nI’m an undergraduate Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), and this contribution is part of a research project involving static analysis of Android apps.\n\nI’m happy to adjust the implementation to better match the project’s architecture, coding conventions, or maintainers’ recommendations.",
